this is hollywood makeup wizard  kevin yeager and these wrinkles on his  face  aren't real they were actually created  with a method called stippling  which deepens the crow's feet around his  eyes  from sculpting enlarged earlobes to  painting broken veins it's just one of  the many ways he can make performers  like keanu reeves look  95 years old kevin draws inspiration  from many classic old age makeup looks  in movies but he gets much of his  material  just by observing people in the real  world when he turned alex winter into  granny preston for bill and ted's bogus  journey back in 1991  he was inspired by his mother-in-law she  had these great  apple cheeks she had that classic granny  look to her face  when he had to make alex and keanu look  like they were 95 years old and bill and  ted face the music  he started with these photoshop concepts  with kian i wanted to give him like an  iggy pop  skinnier older aged rocker look and with  alex i wanted to get in  your friendly disposition every  prosthetic related look  starts with life casts since only alex  and keanu's bare necks  faces and arms were visible on camera  kevin didn't need prosthetics for their  entire bodies  instead only the actors heads and arms  were covered in purple and green  silicone rubbers  the green silicone has an oil in it that  ensures it won't pull any of the actors  hairs out of their bodies  the impressions are then wrapped in  temporary plaster to hold them together  before being cast in hydrocal and  urethane  the life casting process helps a makeup  artist replicate the little details of a  performer's skin  but when it came to alex and keanu's old  age looks the life casts also helped  kevin find and exaggerate wrinkles  already forming on their faces and  forearms just kind of studied their  the lines of their faces and to see  where you know droopage starts  how this jowls will begin to form his  nasolabial folds  becoming more prominent you know his eye  sockets are deepening a slight bit  to mimic the fine details of old skin he  added clay to the busts of alex and  keanu's faces and forearms  which allowed him to sculpt directly on  the skin  this was where kevin could add wrinkles  and veins that really stick out  and different ages don't look the same  while kevin made alex and keanu look 95  here  in the movie blow he made johnny depp  look just a bit older than he already  was aging the actor from his late 30s  into his 60s  as you can see there are still aged  features on his face  but less pronounced the pores on the 95  year old skin  look more elongated something kevin  observed and mimicked while creating  texture  as you get older they begin to stretch  with your skin kevin and his team also  had to create really pronounced wrinkles  for bill and ted  they achieved this by cross hatching all  over the character's forearms and faces  but they changed up their technique on  different parts of the body chin is kind  of funny because it gets a lot of weird  cross hatching wrinkles in them and  wrinkles around the eyes  or crow's feet required a different  pattern too an effect that they could  also achieve through stippling  stippling is done by simply adding a  latex based liquid to the skin  and powdering it it stretches the skin  and causes these wrinkles  kevin used this technique on pete  possible's weight to create wrinkles  around his eyes when the actor had to  play a character who was hundreds of  years old in eon flux  i didn't have to do any age to him as  far as like accentuate all the things i  did to these guys he had a hat in his  face but he was wasn't old enough  the body doesn't just wrinkle as you age  when you get to be 95  your bones begin to show meaning your  sockets get deeper  kevin made sure bone was visible when  sculpting their hands  because bill and ted were so old he also  wanted them to look arthritic  a trait that shows up especially in the  hands you get this curved look i can't  do much about that but what i could do  is exaggerate these knuckles you can see  a fine little bone in between each  knuckle and the knuckles are swollen  and going farther up the arm he even  made the wrist bone stand out  once kevin and his team sculpted all the  details they created another set of  negatives and then poured silicone into  those  molds and sandwiched it all together  silicone is necessary for perfectly  mimicking the translucency and texture  of skin  as you can see here it also naturally  wrinkles like old human skin would  the color of the silicone is already  intrinsically colored to be a flesh tone  and you can see  light through this if i could get that  the right angle  but it's not until additional colors are  added that all the sculpted wrinkles and  bones and pores begin to look  realistic kevin started with a basic  skin color palette of green  and a heavy emphasis on red meanwhile  the thinning hairs punched into keanu's  head weren't a solid gray they were  actually a mix of white and yellow  when looking at the eyes kevin knew that  the color around the eye sockets  darkens with age and airbrushing in  shadow helps the sculpted areas really  pop  making the bone structure much more  visible while veins are usually sculpted  kevin also elevated them through  airbrushing this tool was  especially helpful for the aging veins  on their faces like on  alex and keanu's muscle suits kevin can  airbrush on details like pores  but for their old age he needed to add  even more decay to the skin  these delicate imperfections like these  purple and red capillaries on keanu's  prosthetic nose  needed to be painted by hand he has to  do the same with liver spots but they  are bigger and more noticeable a lot of  them are tiny little breakups little  tiny dots like freckles and then i  most likely hand paint all the all the  liver spots when you get to be bigger  spots like  in some of these pieces i'll actually go  back in and hand paint all the bigger  ones and i'll place those exactly where  i want them to be  tiny aging freckles also make the skin  look older  he found that for some of those he could  easily get lots on at once by taking a  chip brush  and flicking it  for face the music kevin added  additional layers of makeup to the  actors that might seem like  overkill but they really sell the look  and bring out the kinds of aging details  you might never think of  for example when people get older their  noses and ears often enlarge  kevin estimates that he had to make alex  and keanu's ears and noses about  20 bigger than their normal size it  wasn't just the skin that had to look  old  on face the music kevin realized he  could make alex look old by giving him  cataracts  so kevin used these glassy looking  contact lenses that gave alex  foggy eyes now if they were too opaque  alex would have looked blind  while cataracts have more of a milky  look old man  young man well almost young old sort of  young  cold kind of old and by using a simple  combo of glue and thickener  you could apply fake eye bags to keanu  on set  like stickers almost and you just put  them down and you kind of blend the  edges quicker  the attention to both the big details  and especially all those little ones  that only an artist could think of  surprised even the actors themselves  throughout several decades of doing old  age makeup kevin has found the key to  getting it right  knowing that it's imperfect the great  thing about old age makeups is that the  stakes are welcome  they're messy and they're flawed
 

